Oregon, sources say","description":"Former Minnesota safety Koi Perich has committed to Oregon, sources told ESPN on Monday, confirming a report by CBS Sports.","published":"2026-01-13T03:22:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47594926/minnesota-transfer-safety-koi-perich-commits-oregon-ducks-football","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas, Penn St. players lead AP preseason All-America 1st team","description":"Texas edge rusher Colin Simmons is among three Longhorns on The Associated Press All-America team. No. 2 Penn State also had three players, giving the Nittany Lions and Longhorns the most on the team.","published":"2025-08-18T20:05:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46008870/texas-penn-st-players-lead-ap-preseason-all-america-1st-team","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC standardized NIL, revenue sharing contracts 'unfair' for players, agents say","description":"The SEC's new uniform NIL and revenue sharing agreements are causing an uproar among agents concerned that the contracts are loaded with terms that are unfair.","published":"2026-11-20T01:16:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535591/sec-standardized-nil-contracts-unfair-players-agents-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-19T23:50:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft Big Board rankings: Mel Kiper's top 25 prospects, best by position","description":"Six quarterbacks and six receivers ranked in the top 25? Mel Kiper Jr. stacks the best players on the 2027 draft board as of mid-November.","published":"2026-11-19T22:42:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50182998/2027-nfl-draft-rankings-kiper-big-board-top-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr.","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Michigan WR Andrew Marsh facing misdemeanor indecent exposure charge","description":"Michigan receiver Andrew Marsh is facing a misdemeanor charge of indecent exposure stemming from a February incident involving a food service driver.","published":"2026-11-19T21:15:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50533990/michigan-wr-marsh-facing-misdemeanor-indecent-exposure-charge","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-19T21:22:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Hall of Famer Jack Ham returning to broadcast booth after health scare","description":"Hall of Fame linebacker and Penn State radio analyst Jack Ham will return to the broadcast booth on Saturday, just two weeks after suffering a medical emergency.","published":"2026-11-19T19:37:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532925/jack-ham-returning-broadcast-booth-health-scare","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 'College GameDay' Week 12: Virginia Tech vs. Miami","description":"\"College GameDay\" heads to University of Miami for Week 12.","published":"2026-11-19T19:27:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532540/2026-college-gameday-week-12-virginia-tech-vs-miami","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5142588/koi-perich","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Koi Perich","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:51Z","intro":"Koi Perich (born September 26, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Minnesota Golden Gophers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Perich attended Esko High School in Esko, Minnesota. As a junior, he rushed for over 800 yards, notched 75 tackles, two sacks, three interceptions, four forced fumbles, and 25 touchdowns. In the first game of his senior season, Perich intercepted two passes which he returned both for touchdowns. As a senior, he amassed 27 total touchdowns: 16 rushing, five defensive, four return, one passing, and one receiving. Perich also notched 76 tackles, three interceptions, and four fumble recoveries on defense, earning all-state recognition. He accepted an invite to play in the All-American Bowl, where he intercepted a pass on the goal line and blocked a punt en route to earning game MVP honors.\n\nRECRUITING\nPerich received offers from schools such as USC, Michigan, Wisconsin, Minnesota, Iowa and Washington, as well as late offers from Florida State and Ohio State. He committed to play college football for the Minnesota Golden Gophers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman, Perich recorded 24 solo tackles, one pass defended, one forced fumble, and five interceptions. He was named first-team All-Big Ten Conference and second-team All-American following the conclusion of the regular season.\nKoi Perich entered his sophomore season in 2025 with increased responsibilities across defense, special teams, and occasional offensive snaps. Mistakes early in the season led to a reduction of offensive snaps, but Perich scored a game winning touchdown on his first career defensive score to win the schools 2025 homecoming game against Purdue.\nOn January 1, 2026, Perich announced that he would enter the transfer portal.\nOn January 12, 2026, Perich announced that he would be transferring to the University of Oregon."}]}}